# GEMV y = A(256x256) * x(256), LPDDR4 all-bank compute phase.
# LPDDR4_AiM_org has 32 channels x 8 banks = 256 banks.
# Mapping assumption:
# - Logical matrix row = channel_id * 8 + bank_id.
# - Each physical bank uses row 0 only.
# - A 256-wide BF16 row occupies 16 AiM 256b chunks.
# - The 256-element vector is written to the AiM Global Buffer.
# - channel_mask 0xffffffff targets all 32 channels.
# - MAC_ABK 16 expands to 16 column MAC commands across all banks.
# - A full 2KB physical row would be 64 chunks: 64 * 256b = 2KB.
#
# Note: On GDDR6_AiM_org, MAC_ABK would cover 32 channels x 16 banks = 512 banks,
# yet half of them are not doing useful computation.
AiM WR_GB 16 0 0xffffffff
W CFR 0 1
AiM WR_BIAS 64 0xffffffff
AiM MAC_ABK 16 0xffffffff 0
AiM RD_MAC 128 0xffffffff
AiM ISR_EOC
